course: dictionary
lesson: 920
title: Context and dangerous words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. «Bleach» is a good example. In «Never mix bleach with other cleaners», bleach is a strong liquid that cleans and kills germs. Read the words around it, and the meaning becomes clear.
explain: Look for clues. Words like cleaners, poisonous and gas tell you that bleach is a chemical. When you meet a new meaning, swap it into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some sentences are warnings, and the context tells you how to stay safe. «Cleaning products such as bleach must never be drunk, even a little, because they burn the throat.» The words must never and burn show that bleach is not safe to swallow. When you see a warning, read it carefully and follow it.
fact: Bleach is a strong chemical liquid used to kill germs and make things clean and white.
fact: As a verb, to bleach something is to make it white or paler, with chemicals or with sunlight.
fact: «Never mix bleach with other cleaners, because together they can make a poisonous gas.»
fact: Bleach must never be drunk, even a little. The idea that a little bleach is safe to drink is a myth, which means a false belief.
fact: In science, sunlight can bleach colours, and coral bleaching happens when oceans get too warm.
exercise: «Never mix bleach with other cleaners, because together they can make a poisonous gas.» What does this sentence warn you to do? | Mix bleach with cleaners to make them stronger | *Keep bleach apart from other cleaners | Mix them in the bath to make them work faster
exercise: A girl in Kansas hears in a video that a drop of bleach in water cures colds. What is the truth? | *It is a dangerous myth, so never drink bleach | Bleach makes water sweet and safe to drink | Bleach cures colds if you add a drop to water
exercise: «Sunlight can bleach colours.» What does bleach mean in this sentence? | *To make paler | To paint in bright colours | To mix with water | To kill germs
test: «Coral bleaching happens when oceans get too warm.» What does bleaching mean here? | Freezing solid | Being cleaned with bleach | Becoming very deep and dark | *Turning white or paler
test: A child wonders if bleach is safe to drink because a video says so. What is the answer? | Yes, but only if it is in a cup | *No, bleach is poisonous if swallowed, and the idea is a myth | No, but only if it is cold | Yes, a little bleach is healthy
exam: Why must bleach be kept locked away from children, in its own bottle? | Because it smells of flowers and children like it | *Because it can burn skin and eyes and is poisonous if swallowed | Because it makes children grow faster | Because it is a food that goes off quickly
